\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   Fill Thou my life, O Lord my God,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  In every part with praise,
\par  That my whole being may proclaim
\par  Thy being and Thy ways.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  Not for the lip of praise alone,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0   Nor e'en the praising heart,
\par   I ask but for a life made up,
\par  Of praise in every part:
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.   Praise in the common things of life,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0   Its goings out and in;
\par   Praise in each duty and each deed,
\par   However small and mean.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. Fill every part of me with praise
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Let all my being speak
\par Of thee and of Thy love, O Lord,
\par Poor though I be and weak.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  So shalt Thou, Lord from me, e'en me
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Receive the glory due:
\par And so shall I begin on earth
\par the song for ever new.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6.  So shall no part of day or night
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 From sacredness be free;
\par But all my life, in every step,
\par \pard     Be fellowship with Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

